<td>
<p><iframe title="allied health ltcc student video" src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/Ju5Lxan5Jm8" width="400" height="315" frameborder="0" allowfullscreen="allowfullscreen"></iframe></p>
<p><span>College offer students the opportunity to gain fundamental skills in a career field by completing an intensive course or set of courses. Upon successful completion of one of these programs, the student will receive a department-issued certificate. These programs differ from the college's official certificates of achievement in that they are short-term, cover a more narrow area of study, and are generally not recorded on the student's transcript. These programs are coordinated by the individual departments. Interested students should contact the CTE Department for further information.</span>&nbsp;</p>
